      "answer": "10",
      "reason_rejected": "This answer adds the 4 years of college to the 6 years of post-college earning. However, the question asks 'how long would it take to earn the money equivalent', which refers to the duration of the earning period required to recoup the costs, not the total elapsed time from the start of the decision. The 4 years of college are the period where the debt was incurred and income lost, not the period where it is being earned back."
    },
    {
      "answer": "4",
      "reason_rejected": "This assumes the full new salary ($75,000) is used to pay back the 'lost' money. This is incorrect because the baseline salary ($25,000) would have been earned anyway had he not gone to college; only the *incremental* income ($50,000) covers the opportunity cost and debt."
    }
